# tools/al/ales_rack_rename_witness.rish — a slot re-named in place (ALES36).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES36.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260814/20260814-152510_fill-ales36-lotus-rack-rename.md
# Stands on: lotus/rack.rye (ALES30) — the Rack, its named Slots, find / name_of, and the naming invariant, reused whole.
#
# lotus/rack_rename.rye re-names a slot in place: keep the held audio exactly where it is and change only the name. The crux: renaming
# `from` to `to` re-names exactly one slot in place — the held audio and every OTHER slot untouched — and preserves ALES30's naming
# invariant that a name names at most one slot. A rack.Slot holds its name and its audio in SEPARATE storage, so overwriting the name
# buffer cannot touch the held samples; the rename resolves `from` to one index, checks `to` against every OTHER slot for a collision,
# and rewrites only that slot's name bytes. The selftest proves: a renamed slot answers to its new name with the same audio
# byte-for-byte and the old name is gone; a same-name rename is a clean no-op; a collision refuses Duplicate; an absent `from` refuses
# NoSlot; an empty or oversized `to` refuses BadName — the rack untouched in every refusal. Purely local — no signature, no keys, no
# network, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_rack_rename_witness.rish

say "ales-rack-rename: Language EN — ALES36 gives Lotus the rename in place: a name typed in haste is wrong, or a merge brought in a stem whose name a keeper wants to change, and rename fixes it without dropping and re-filing the span — it keeps the held audio exactly where it is and changes only the name."
say "ales-rack-rename: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: renaming `from` to `to` re-names exactly one slot in place — the held audio and every other slot untouched — and preserves ALES30's naming invariant that a name names at most one slot; renaming a slot to its own name is a clean no-op."
say "ales-rack-rename: Lens TAME — a rack.Slot holds its name and its audio in separate storage, so overwriting the name buffer cannot touch the held samples; the collision check excludes the slot being renamed (so a same-name rename is not a false Duplicate); rack.find / name_of reused whole, RackRenameError = rack.RackError names no new fault; siloed to lotus/, no signature, no key, no network, no funds, no device, no meter, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/rack_rename"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/rack_rename.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-rack-rename: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/rack_rename.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-rack-rename: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-rack-rename: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-rack-rename' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-rack-rename: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-rack-rename line"

say "ales-rack-rename: GREEN — a keeper fixes a mistyped slot name without dropping and re-filing the span: rename re-names exactly one slot in place, the held audio and every other slot untouched, refusing Duplicate on a collision, NoSlot on an absent name, and BadName on a bad target. With rename the purely-local rack primitives are complete (file, paste, drop, save, seal, load, merge, rename); the next purely-local rung is a session file carrying more than one rack. The SIGNED carry (via a Kumara key) and the ALES0-wire carry stay module seams for Keaton's word."
